# Classes the Rust side owns that the worker still resolves to the real Composer implementation,
# so no guard is emitted for them. An entry belongs here only when the worker has a mechanism that
# makes a natively constructed instance correct; without one the class must be guarded, or code
# running here would silently work on an instance the Rust side never sees. One FQCN per line,
# each with the mechanism that justifies it.

# The wire codec revives values of this class from the object record serialize() writes for them
# (php/runtime/Shirabe/MaterializedValue.php), so the real declaration has to stay loadable.
Composer\Package\Link

# The wire codec revives values of this class from the object record serialize() writes for them
# (php/runtime/Shirabe/MaterializedValue.php), so the real declaration has to stay loadable.
Composer\Util\Http\Response

# Plugins subclass this class to provide their own installers. An instance is constructed by the
# plugin and lives only in the worker; the Rust side reaches it solely through the
# InstallerInterface reverse adapter once the plugin registers it with the InstallationManager.
# Every service it holds (IO, Composer, DownloadManager, Filesystem, repositories, packages) is a
# proxy stub, so the real implementation works on the entities the Rust side owns, and the
# subclass's overrides see PHP's late binding of $this.
Composer\Installer\LibraryInstaller

# Constructed by the real LibraryInstaller above for the same plugin-owned instance; it holds
# only proxy stubs (IO, Filesystem) and its own configuration strings.
Composer\Installer\BinaryInstaller

# A static-only helper the real LibraryInstaller and BinaryInstaller above call. It keeps no
# entity the Rust side owns: its answers derive from the worker process's environment and OS.
# TODO(php-runtime): environment overrides the Rust side makes with Platform::putEnv after the
# worker started are not visible to this copy.
Composer\Util\Platform
